<title>JAPAN: Japan March cocoa bean imports up 14.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan March cocoa bean imports up 14.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in March totalled 5,733 tonnes, up 14.3 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Mar 97	  Feb 97	 Mar 96</p>
<p> Total		5,733	   5,539	  5,017</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		4,628	   4,276	  4,077</p>
<p> Venezuela	    355		50	    111</p>
<p> Ecuador		388	     158	    148</p>
<p> Brazil		 297	     474	    237</p>
<p> Malaysia		25	     175	    315</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first three months of calendar 1997 were 17,211 tonnes against 12,823 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Mar 97	 Feb 97	  Mar 96</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	     66	    99	     185</p>
<p> Cocoa butter	 1,699	 1,708	   1,495</p>
<p> Cocoa powder	   729	   710	   1,500</p>
<p>Chocolate</p>
<p>  confectionery	 825	   871	     926</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
